WEBVTT

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.270
Good morning.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.569
You're in a good mood.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.633
It's another beautiful
day in the Delta Quadrant.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.804
What'd you have
for breakfast?

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.278
I'll see you tonight.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.412
Here you are, Lieutenant.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.548
Thank you.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.986
Nice job, Ensign.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.968
You keep the warp field
that stable,

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.128
you might just get us home
a few years early.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.202
The Starfleet Manual

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.176
allows for a variance of.3.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.974
That's only a guideline.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.605
You can do better.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.982
I don't remember giving you
permission to work here.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.489
I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.923
I'm helping him study
warp mechanics.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.824
You should have notified me.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.487
It's a busy day, and I...

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.791
Lieutenant.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.559
I'm fine.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.231
I'm detecting another life sign.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.174
Where?

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.677
Inside Lieutenant Torres.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.543
It could be a parasite.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.751
Seven of Nine to the Doctor.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.948
Go ahead.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.717
I'll be accompanying
Lieutenant Torres

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.951
to Sick Bay.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:33.957
What's wrong?

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.620
I believe she's pregnant.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.181
The fetus appears
to be about seven weeks old

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.649
and doing quite well.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.844
So are you.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.615
Why did she faint?

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.351
Klingon and human metabolisms
sometimes clash.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.449
Tell me about it.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.517
It's not uncommon
for such pregnancies

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:52.258
to cause biochemical
fluctuations in the mother.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.356
Is that serious?

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.627
Not usually.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.966
You can expect
some behavioral volatility,

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.437
increased nutritional needs.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.134
Creating new life is a big job.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.372
Hmm. "Creating new life."

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.346
I can't believe it.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.473
I don't mean to be indelicate,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.348
but weren't you trying
to get pregnant?

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.887
Well... of course.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:19.516
I mean... well, we knew
we wanted a family.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.492
But the odds against
human-Klingon conception

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.493
are so high.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.494
Well, apparently

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.723
you've beaten the odds.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.458
May I be the first
to congratulate you?

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.625
When is the baby due?

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.296
Normally, Klingon pregnancies
run 30 weeks,

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:35.170
but with mixed species,
it could be sooner.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.300
Is it a girl or a boy?

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.639
No. Don't tell.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.804
Uh, I want to be surprised.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.440
Ah. We've already
been surprised.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:47.043
I just don't see any reason
to have to label the baby.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.178
I don't want to know
the gender.

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.653
I don't want to have
to pick a name yet.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.747
Okay, okay.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.416
Mommy knows best.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.859
"Mommy"?

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.591
I wonder if the holodeck
has any child-rearing programs.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:04.102
There are some things
you just can't simulate.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.899
I will take whatever
help I can get.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.495
We should get our
quarters ready.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.905
Maybe I can replicate
one of those antique cribs.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.034
And put it where?

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.203
We'll need to rearrange
the living area.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:15.440
We need to do
a lot more than that.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.278
You're happy
about this, right?

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.183
Of course I'm happy.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.914
Just a little overwhelmed,
that's all.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.285
Me, too.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:26.689
Can we, uh, keep this
to ourselves for a while?

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.021
Absolutely.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.664
I, uh... I need to get to work.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:40.898
See you later... Dad.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.074
Congratulations, Tom.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.381
Thanks. How did you find out?

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.716
Icheb.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.951
Oh, he wasn't
supposed to tell?

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.458
Well, we were hoping
to keep it private...

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.893
for an hour or so.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:08.899
As they say on Talax,
Omara s'alas...

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:11.492
"Good news has no clothes."

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.763
Thanks... I guess.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:17.071
Mm. Now, my good news
would be learning

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.906
that I'll be the godfather.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:22.379
I do have experience
with Naomi Wildman, you know.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.110
I can't think of anyone
more qualified.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:29.518
Well, in that case, I've been
making up a list of names.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:30.556
Tell me...

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.092
Have you checked
the warp core

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.525
for radiation leaks today?

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:37.495
No. Why?

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.964
You have a certain...
glow about you.

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:44.937
Okay, who told you?

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.437
I just heard.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.371
Congratulations.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.609
Thanks.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.303
Seven said you were dizzy.
Are you all right?

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.640
I'm fine.

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.840
Nothing ever rattled her,
not even the Cardassians.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:56.939
This is scarier.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.277
Would you like some time off?

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.943
To do what?

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:00.950
Adjust.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.645
This is a big change.

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:05.020
I'll work during the day,
sleep at night,

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:06.991
and have the baby
when it's time.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.890
Well, if you need to
cut back on your duties,

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.256
I'm sure Seven would be happy

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.762
to fill in for you.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:13.822
I think I can handle it.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.424
Congratulations, buddy.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.594
Where did you hear the news?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.001
In the datastream
from Earth?

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.003
Actually, I think

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.300
it was a transmission
from the Borg.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:23.842
It's all over now.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.775
No more late nights
on the holodeck.

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.437
No more racing
the Delta Flyer.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:30.175
Don't you think you're
exaggerating just a little?

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.443
I've seen it happen.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:33.781
The new dad gets
tied down with family.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.115
Old friends drop away.

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.816
It's fatherhood, Harry,
not exile.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.050
If you say so.

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:41.650
Kidding aside, how's it feel?

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.695
Well, it's...

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:47.164
It's not quite real yet.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:49.258
Maybe that's
what pregnancy's for.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:53.032
Time to let reality sink in...

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.335
before your life
spins out of control.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:09.477
You need any help?

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:13.116
Mr. Paris, this may
be the first time

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.285
you've ever volunteered
to assist me.

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.828
Really?

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.887
Well, we ought to change that.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.057
I mean, we've known each other
a long time.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.600
We ought to work more closely.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.397
I'll keep that in mind.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.462
So I guess you've heard

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.906
B'Elanna and I are going
to have a baby.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:32.067
I was unaware.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:35.238
Oh. Finally, someone
who doesn't know.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.511
Allow me to extend
my best wishes.

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.245
Thanks.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:43.254
You know, a baby is, uh...

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:46.814
it's a big responsibility,

00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:48.724
but I'm ready for it.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:52.662
Not that, uh, you can ever be
completely ready.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.359
Can you?

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:59.894
Lieutenant, are you asking me
for advice about fatherhood?

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:02.702
Well, I don't know anyone else
who's been through it.

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:06.074
I'm afraid my parenting skills
are somewhat dormant.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:09.342
It's been many years
since my children were young.

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:12.748
Well then, you've had a long
time to think back on it.

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:14.046
Any helpful hints?

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:18.113
Offspring can be
disturbingly illogical,

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.182
yet profoundly fulfilling.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.889
You should anticipate paradox.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:28.229
Ah. I'll remember that.

00:09:28.301 --> 00:09:31.395
If you'd like my counsel
on more specific issues...

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.837
Something tells me
I'm going to be volunteering

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:37.137
to work with you
on a regular basis.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:48.413
So?

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:49.886
Looks nice.

00:09:49.956 --> 00:09:54.222
Well, I figured
quiet, romantic dinners

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:56.659
may soon be
a thing of the past.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.355
Tough day?

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:04.699
The Captain practically
relieved me of duty...

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.465
as if I couldn't handle
being an engineer

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:08.029
and being pregnant
at the same time.

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:09.938
Well, if you
ever need a baby-sitter,

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:12.567
"Godfather Neelix"
is ready to go.

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:14.374
Chakotay wants to be godfather.

00:10:14.447 --> 00:10:16.438
Well, Neelix already has
a list of names.

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:19.211
Now, I don't mind people
suggesting names.

00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:22.277
What annoys me is
all of the free advice

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:24.448
about feeding, discipline.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:26.115
Folk wisdom is my favorite.

00:10:26.192 --> 00:10:28.319
According to Chell,
Bolians believe

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.794
that if you give birth
near a warp core

00:10:30.863 --> 00:10:33.161
it'll improve
the baby's disposition.

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:34.426
Why does everybody feel

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.331
they're entitled
to give us advice?

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:37.369
This is our child.

00:10:37.436 --> 00:10:38.835
Well, people
should know better

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:40.929
than to interfere
with a Klingon mother.

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:42.736
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.207
Nothing. It was a joke.

00:10:44.276 --> 00:10:45.675
What does being Klingon

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:46.803
have to do with it?

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:47.903
Hey, take it easy.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.470
I don't want to take it easy.

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:52.108
I want everybody to back off
and just let me...

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.881
The Doctor said
I might experience

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:01.586
some behavioral volatility.

00:11:01.661 --> 00:11:04.027
I guess this is it.

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:07.122
Well, forget about the Doctor.

00:11:07.199 --> 00:11:12.068
Forget the Captain
and all the godfathers.

00:11:12.138 --> 00:11:13.127
Maybe you're right.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.331
I know I am.

00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:18.571
This isn't about
their expectations or hopes

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.875
or... doubts.

00:11:21.947 --> 00:11:24.472
None of this belongs to them.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.075
It belongs to us.

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:30.212
All of it.

00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:31.916
Lucky us.

00:11:31.991 --> 00:11:34.926
Lieutenants Torres and Paris

00:11:34.994 --> 00:11:36.791
please report to Sick Bay.

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:44.328
It's a holographic extrapolation
of your child's spine,

00:11:44.403 --> 00:11:45.927
approximately ten months
after birth.

00:11:46.005 --> 00:11:47.336
It's deviated.

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.636
Yes. There's a pronounced
curvature to the left.

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:50.937
Can it be corrected?

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:53.410
I had surgery for it
when I was a baby.

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:54.844
You never told me that.

00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:56.313
My mother had it, too.

00:11:56.382 --> 00:11:58.577
It tends to run
in Klingon families,

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:00.380
especially among females.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.453
Are you saying
that this baby is a girl?

00:12:04.523 --> 00:12:05.922
No, I didn't say that.

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:07.515
But it is a girl, right?

00:12:07.593 --> 00:12:09.458
You cannot infer that.

00:12:09.528 --> 00:12:11.496
It's okay. You might
as well just tell us.

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:14.023
Yes.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.499
It's a girl...

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:18.935
and aside from
the deviated spine,

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:20.494
she's healthy.

00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:23.133
Will she need surgery?

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:25.143
Fortunately,
we've advanced beyond that.

00:12:25.211 --> 00:12:27.645
Genetic modification
is the treatment of choice.

00:12:27.713 --> 00:12:31.274
If you can project
an image of the spine,

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.784
can you use the genetic data

00:12:33.853 --> 00:12:36.185
to show us the whole baby?

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.348
I could.

00:12:39.425 --> 00:12:41.586
L-it would only be
an approximation.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.719
Let's take a look.

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:44.728
I don't know.

00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:45.729
Oh, come on.

00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:47.231
Aren't you curious?

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:50.328
Okay.

00:13:03.582 --> 00:13:05.015
Oh, she's beautiful.

00:13:05.084 --> 00:13:07.552
Forehead ridges?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.247
Yes.

00:13:09.321 --> 00:13:11.846
But she's only
one-quarter Klingon.

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:14.449
Klingon traits remain dominant
for several generations,

00:13:14.527 --> 00:13:15.858
even with a single ancestor.

00:13:15.928 --> 00:13:19.091
Oh, she looks just
like her mother.

00:13:22.568 --> 00:13:24.593
You are so much
like your mother.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.503
She's perfect...

00:13:29.241 --> 00:13:31.106
isn't she?

00:13:43.189 --> 00:13:45.657
Oh, what a day.

00:13:45.724 --> 00:13:47.055
Mm-hmm.

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:48.923
Six years in
the Delta Quadrant

00:13:48.994 --> 00:13:50.393
and nothing has ever
scared me as much

00:13:50.462 --> 00:13:52.555
as hearing our baby
had a problem.

00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:54.189
It's not much of a problem.

00:13:54.266 --> 00:13:55.961
Well, we didn't know that
at first.

00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:57.798
Now we know.

00:13:58.938 --> 00:14:01.236
And we also know that the Doctor

00:14:01.307 --> 00:14:05.209
is going to fix everything
tomorrow morning.

00:14:06.312 --> 00:14:07.870
I'm sorry.

00:14:07.947 --> 00:14:10.677
It's a lot to take in
all at once,

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:12.876
and I'm really tired.

00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:15.512
We could both
use some sleep.

00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:18.352
Computer, dim the lights.

00:14:22.728 --> 00:14:24.662
Somebody make sure

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.163
those coals
are completely out.

00:14:26.232 --> 00:14:28.063
I'll get it, Dad.

00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:29.532
You kids be careful

00:14:29.602 --> 00:14:31.331
and be back before sunset.

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:33.337
And bring your appetites...
we're having fish for dinner.

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:34.872
If you two
can catch any.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.931
Dad, I increased
the field strength

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:38.407
of the targeting lure.

00:14:38.477 --> 00:14:42.243
Ooh, those fish
don't stand a chance.

00:14:42.314 --> 00:14:43.406
You better get going.

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:45.279
Your cousins aren't
going to wait forever.

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:46.545
I was thinking...

00:14:46.619 --> 00:14:48.849
maybe I could go fishing
with you and Uncle Carl.

00:14:48.921 --> 00:14:51.355
I thought you were
looking forward to the hike?

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:52.447
Just the kids.

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:53.889
No dads to slow you down.

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:56.587
They don't like me.

00:14:56.662 --> 00:14:58.527
Why would you say that?

00:14:58.597 --> 00:15:00.565
Because it's true.

00:15:00.633 --> 00:15:02.191
Come on, B'Elanna, let's go.

00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:05.092
See?

00:15:07.673 --> 00:15:09.334
Now, go on.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:10.636
Have a good time.

00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:11.733
Dad?

00:15:12.811 --> 00:15:14.836
What is it?

00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:17.508
Nothing.

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:30.522
Relax.

00:15:30.596 --> 00:15:31.858
We're not that late.

00:15:31.931 --> 00:15:33.831
The Doctor
scheduled me at 0800.

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:36.527
You still have time for my
favorite gourmet breakfast...

00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:37.660
peanut butter toast.

00:15:37.736 --> 00:15:38.930
I'm too tired to eat.

00:15:39.071 --> 00:15:40.663
Well, if you're having
trouble sleeping now,

00:15:40.739 --> 00:15:42.934
wait till those
0200 feedings come around.

00:15:43.008 --> 00:15:44.339
You'll be in charge of those.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.537
I can't wait.

00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:49.945
Look, uh, you don't
have to come with me.

00:15:50.049 --> 00:15:51.949
It's a minor procedure.

00:15:52.017 --> 00:15:55.077
Wouldn't you like
some moral support?

00:15:55.154 --> 00:15:57.213
I'm not an invalid.

00:15:57.289 --> 00:16:00.452
Well, in that case,
you're on your own.

00:16:00.526 --> 00:16:02.426
That goes for breakfast, too.

00:16:06.031 --> 00:16:08.659
I've been expanding my database
in obstetrics and pediatrics.

00:16:08.734 --> 00:16:10.634
You haven't found another
problem, have you?

00:16:10.703 --> 00:16:11.727
No, not at all,

00:16:11.804 --> 00:16:12.896
but I have put together

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:14.630
a prenatal enrichment program.

00:16:14.707 --> 00:16:16.334
Why am I not surprised?

00:16:16.408 --> 00:16:19.206
I'd like to start with
trans-abdominal vocalization.

00:16:19.278 --> 00:16:20.370
Let me guess.

00:16:20.446 --> 00:16:21.845
You're going to
sing to my fetus.

00:16:21.914 --> 00:16:23.211
Through a diatonal amplifier.

00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:24.613
It's quite safe,
and it should

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:26.514
enhance the child's
mathematical abilities.

00:16:26.585 --> 00:16:28.143
Can we talk
about this later?

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.346
Absolutely...

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:31.548
at our first
parenting class.

00:16:31.623 --> 00:16:32.920
Parenting class.

00:16:33.058 --> 00:16:34.855
Birthing techniques,
feeding options,

00:16:34.927 --> 00:16:35.859
bonding strategies.

00:16:35.928 --> 00:16:36.917
It's not all hard work, though.

00:16:37.062 --> 00:16:38.461
We'll have ample time for fun.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.656
Could we get on with it?

00:16:39.732 --> 00:16:42.326
Certainly.

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:44.369
Computer, dim lights.

00:16:44.436 --> 00:16:46.927
I hope you don't expect me
to sleep through this.

00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:48.200
Of course not.

00:16:48.273 --> 00:16:50.707
The darkness encourages
vascular dilation.

00:16:50.776 --> 00:16:52.835
Now, you may feel
a slight tingling.

00:16:52.911 --> 00:16:54.970
Please remain as
still as possible.

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.642
B'Elanna, come have lunch.

00:17:00.719 --> 00:17:01.686
That's okay.

00:17:01.754 --> 00:17:02.686
I'm not hungry.

00:17:02.755 --> 00:17:04.017
You better eat while you can.

00:17:04.089 --> 00:17:06.387
You know our dads aren't
going to catch any fish.

00:17:14.433 --> 00:17:15.798
Here.

00:17:15.868 --> 00:17:16.800
Thanks.

00:17:16.869 --> 00:17:17.801
Your mom wasn't sure

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:18.996
you'd be able
to come this weekend.

00:17:19.071 --> 00:17:20.800
I had a lot of schoolwork.

00:17:20.873 --> 00:17:22.170
Well, I'm glad you made it.

00:17:22.241 --> 00:17:23.902
That's nice of you to say.

00:17:23.976 --> 00:17:25.307
Hey, B'Elanna, can
you hand me a drink?

00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:26.708
Okay.

00:17:28.781 --> 00:17:30.715
Thanks.

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:39.152
My teacher said Klingons
like live food.

00:17:39.224 --> 00:17:41.215
Hey, stop it! Stop.

00:17:41.293 --> 00:17:43.454
It was just a joke.

00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:44.897
It was a stupid joke, Dean.

00:17:44.963 --> 00:17:47.227
He's always doing stuff
like that to me.

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.567
Don't be mad, B'Elanna.

00:17:49.635 --> 00:17:51.603
B'Elanna, wait!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.228
Computer, raise lights.

00:17:56.809 --> 00:17:58.606
Your daughter's spinal column

00:17:58.677 --> 00:18:00.235
is now perfectly aligned.

00:18:00.312 --> 00:18:01.506
Is she going to be all right?

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.842
Better than all right

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:05.110
if her parents
are any indication.

00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:20.390
Computer, access
B'Elanna Torres' medical file.

00:18:20.466 --> 00:18:22.593
File accessed.

00:18:22.668 --> 00:18:26.229
Project a holographic image
of the baby.

00:18:29.975 --> 00:18:32.739
Now, extrapolate what
the child's facial features

00:18:32.811 --> 00:18:36.804
will look like...
at 12 years old.

00:18:44.823 --> 00:18:48.486
Display the fetus genome.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.120
Delete the following
gene sequences.

00:18:54.867 --> 00:18:57.495
Extrapolate what
the child would look like

00:18:57.569 --> 00:18:59.161
with those genetic changes.

00:19:04.176 --> 00:19:06.235
Delete the following sequences.

00:19:09.014 --> 00:19:10.743
Extrapolate.

00:19:25.397 --> 00:19:27.729
Save changes.

00:19:29.234 --> 00:19:31.896
Restrict access to this file;

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:34.063
B'Elanna Torres only.

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:42.905
There's no valid
medical reason

00:19:42.981 --> 00:19:44.175
to do what you're proposing.

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:45.181
I disagree.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.741
You want to delete
entire DNA sequences.

00:19:47.819 --> 00:19:50.583
The genes that create
redundant organs, for example.

00:19:50.656 --> 00:19:51.680
They're superfluous.

00:19:51.757 --> 00:19:54.021
Those redundancies
are there for a reason.

00:19:54.092 --> 00:19:56.526
Does my daughter need
a third lung to survive?

00:19:56.595 --> 00:19:59.257
Strictly speaking, no,
but having it may be beneficial.

00:19:59.331 --> 00:20:01.595
Some geneticists believe
the extra lung evolved

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:04.192
to give Klingons greater stamina
on the battlefield.

00:20:04.269 --> 00:20:06.931
My daughter is not going
to be a Klingon warrior.

00:20:07.005 --> 00:20:08.597
With all due respect,
you have no idea

00:20:08.674 --> 00:20:10.073
what your daughter's
going to be!

00:20:13.111 --> 00:20:15.545
What if she develops
an interest in athletics?

00:20:15.614 --> 00:20:17.946
Greater lung capacity
would be an advantage.

00:20:18.016 --> 00:20:19.677
The point is, there's no reason

00:20:19.751 --> 00:20:21.719
to arbitrarily remove
genetic traits.

00:20:21.787 --> 00:20:23.379
It's not arbitrary!

00:20:23.455 --> 00:20:24.945
It's preventive.

00:20:25.023 --> 00:20:26.115
How so?

00:20:26.191 --> 00:20:27.249
That third lung could

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:28.588
become diseased, couldn't it?

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.592
I suppose.

00:20:29.661 --> 00:20:30.685
Then what I'm suggesting

00:20:30.762 --> 00:20:31.956
is no different than

00:20:32.097 --> 00:20:34.224
removing an appendix
before it becomes inflamed.

00:20:34.299 --> 00:20:36.529
Why tamper with
biological systems

00:20:36.602 --> 00:20:38.160
that have evolved over eons?

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:40.569
Like curvature of the spine?

00:20:44.109 --> 00:20:47.840
If I make these changes,
it'll affect her appearance.

00:20:47.913 --> 00:20:50.074
I'm aware of that.

00:20:50.148 --> 00:20:51.445
Are you also aware

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:55.976
that some of these genes
influence behavior, personality?

00:20:56.054 --> 00:20:58.818
None of that's as important
as her health.

00:21:01.126 --> 00:21:03.117
What does Tom think
about all this?

00:21:03.195 --> 00:21:05.925
I wanted to see
what you thought first.

00:21:05.998 --> 00:21:08.296
Well, as you can see,
I'm very dubious.

00:21:08.367 --> 00:21:12.701
Look, I've done statistical
analyses, epidemiology.

00:21:12.771 --> 00:21:14.932
At least review my work.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.338
All right, I'll look at it.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.678
But in the meantime...

00:21:22.147 --> 00:21:25.310
I suggest you have a talk
with your husband.

00:21:25.417 --> 00:21:27.112
Absolutely not.

00:21:27.185 --> 00:21:29.949
This is our child's health
we're talking about.

00:21:30.022 --> 00:21:31.455
No, it's more than that.

00:21:31.523 --> 00:21:33.684
You want to change who she is.

00:21:33.759 --> 00:21:36.455
Her individuality, her...

00:21:40.532 --> 00:21:43.160
You don't want her
to be Klingon.

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:46.966
That's what this is
really about, isn't it?

00:21:47.039 --> 00:21:48.063
You're trying

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.539
to protect her
from being Klingon,

00:21:49.608 --> 00:21:51.735
because you had a rough time
when you were a kid.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:54.938
I was treated like a monster.

00:21:55.013 --> 00:21:57.880
That isn't going to happen
to our daughter.

00:21:57.949 --> 00:22:01.885
Everyone on Voyager will accept
her for who she really is.

00:22:01.953 --> 00:22:04.046
That's easy for you to say.
You're human.

00:22:04.122 --> 00:22:05.885
Meaning what, exactly?

00:22:05.957 --> 00:22:09.518
Meaning you don't
understand what it's like.

00:22:10.796 --> 00:22:14.254
Okay, then... tell me.

00:22:14.333 --> 00:22:18.531
When the people around you
are all one way and you're not,

00:22:18.603 --> 00:22:20.468
you can't help feeling

00:22:20.539 --> 00:22:23.770
like there's
something wrong with you.

00:22:23.842 --> 00:22:27.334
But Voyager isn't just one way.

00:22:27.412 --> 00:22:29.573
We've got Bajorans, Vulcans

00:22:29.648 --> 00:22:31.548
a Talaxian...

00:22:31.616 --> 00:22:33.743
And 140 humans.

00:22:33.819 --> 00:22:36.481
Our daughter is going
to have a mixed heritage,

00:22:36.555 --> 00:22:37.783
just like her mother.

00:22:37.856 --> 00:22:39.915
It's something
you'll have in common,

00:22:39.991 --> 00:22:41.856
something she should
be proud of.

00:22:41.927 --> 00:22:42.916
Why destroy that?

00:22:42.994 --> 00:22:45.121
I'm not destroying anything!

00:22:45.197 --> 00:22:47.757
Gene resequencing
isn't a weapon.

00:22:47.833 --> 00:22:50.461
It's a tool...
like a hyperspanner!

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:53.766
She's not a machine.
She's our daughter.

00:22:55.707 --> 00:22:58.301
I'm not exactly sure
what you want me to do.

00:22:58.377 --> 00:22:59.901
I want you to
order the Doctor

00:22:59.978 --> 00:23:01.536
to genetically
alter my child.

00:23:01.613 --> 00:23:03.638
Do you see what I'm
dealing with here?

00:23:03.715 --> 00:23:06.479
What you're asking for
is ethically questionable.

00:23:06.551 --> 00:23:09.748
The Doctor has reservations,
your husband is against it.

00:23:09.821 --> 00:23:12.221
I only want to do
what you did...

00:23:13.291 --> 00:23:15.054
...for Seven of Nine.

00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:17.357
I beg your pardon?

00:23:17.429 --> 00:23:19.056
You had her implants removed.

00:23:19.131 --> 00:23:20.689
I don't see the connection.

00:23:20.766 --> 00:23:22.290
You altered her physiology.

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.096
You changed who she was.

00:23:24.169 --> 00:23:26.399
I was acting
in her best interests.

00:23:26.471 --> 00:23:27.403
That's all I'm doing.

00:23:27.472 --> 00:23:28.404
Seven was born human.

00:23:28.473 --> 00:23:30.407
The Captain just helped

00:23:30.475 --> 00:23:31.806
to restore her
original physiology.

00:23:31.877 --> 00:23:33.504
And gave her a much better
life in the process.

00:23:33.578 --> 00:23:34.772
Our child isn't even born yet.

00:23:34.846 --> 00:23:36.871
How do you know what's going
to make her life better?

00:23:36.948 --> 00:23:39.212
I just don't want her
to start at a disadvantage.

00:23:39.284 --> 00:23:42.185
Look, the Doctor said you might
experience mood swings...

00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:43.778
That's it.
Just dismiss my argument

00:23:43.855 --> 00:23:45.379
as some kind
of hormonal outburst!

00:23:45.457 --> 00:23:46.651
I didn't mean that!

00:23:46.725 --> 00:23:48.693
Stop it, both of you.

00:23:53.031 --> 00:23:56.057
The biggest problem
you two have isn't ethical...

00:23:56.134 --> 00:23:58.125
it's marital.

00:23:58.203 --> 00:24:00.899
I'm happy to offer
you advice as a friend,

00:24:00.972 --> 00:24:02.200
but as your Captain,

00:24:02.274 --> 00:24:04.902
I am not going to overrule
the Chief Medical Officer.

00:24:05.043 --> 00:24:06.738
You two need to work this out.

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:14.043
B'Elanna...

00:24:14.119 --> 00:24:15.416
What?

00:24:15.487 --> 00:24:16.886
You heard the Captain.

00:24:16.955 --> 00:24:18.013
We have to work this out.

00:24:18.089 --> 00:24:19.283
There's nothing to work out.

00:24:19.357 --> 00:24:20.585
You're getting what you want.

00:24:20.659 --> 00:24:21.626
What I want is to have

00:24:21.693 --> 00:24:23.285
a civilized discussion
with my wife.

00:24:24.329 --> 00:24:25.694
Maybe a change
of scenery would help.

00:24:25.764 --> 00:24:26.628
How about the holodeck?

00:24:26.698 --> 00:24:28.029
That's your solution
to everything.

00:24:28.099 --> 00:24:29.066
At least I'm trying.

00:24:29.134 --> 00:24:30.761
Look, I don't care
where we do it,

00:24:30.836 --> 00:24:32.360
but we have to talk
this out...

00:24:32.437 --> 00:24:33.495
I am tired of talking,

00:24:33.572 --> 00:24:35.096
all right?

00:24:51.623 --> 00:24:53.887
Do I need a reservation?

00:24:53.959 --> 00:24:55.551
What happened?

00:24:55.627 --> 00:24:57.959
I think B'Elanna and I
need some time apart.

00:24:58.063 --> 00:25:00.122
My couch is your couch.

00:25:03.869 --> 00:25:05.063
She's barely pregnant

00:25:05.136 --> 00:25:07.468
and already we're having
a major crisis.

00:25:07.539 --> 00:25:09.234
You'll make up. You always do.

00:25:09.307 --> 00:25:10.831
Yeah, but that's what
worries me.

00:25:10.909 --> 00:25:12.604
We're always fighting
and making up.

00:25:12.677 --> 00:25:14.645
How's that going
to affect our daughter?

00:25:14.713 --> 00:25:16.613
She's going to have
a great life.

00:25:16.681 --> 00:25:18.615
Piloting the ship from your lap,

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:20.913
battling Dr. Chaotica
on the holodeck.

00:25:21.019 --> 00:25:24.785
Yeah, unless B'Elanna thinks
battling is too Klingon.

00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:27.381
She's always been sensitive
about being part Klingon.

00:25:27.459 --> 00:25:28.517
You know that.

00:25:28.593 --> 00:25:29.924
That doesn't give her the right

00:25:30.028 --> 00:25:32.019
to turn our child
into a science experiment.

00:25:32.097 --> 00:25:35.396
But it does explain why
this is so important to her.

00:25:37.469 --> 00:25:39.130
What am I supposed to do?

00:25:40.539 --> 00:25:42.769
Maybe you should tell
her you understand.

00:25:42.841 --> 00:25:44.206
What good would that do?

00:25:45.977 --> 00:25:47.672
It might make her
less defensive,

00:25:47.746 --> 00:25:49.441
and then maybe
it would be easier

00:25:49.514 --> 00:25:51.277
for her to see
your point of view.

00:25:51.349 --> 00:25:54.944
Yeah? What if she can't?

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:58.950
Like I said,
my couch is your couch.

00:26:16.608 --> 00:26:18.473
She should be back by now.

00:26:18.543 --> 00:26:21.137
Nobody has any idea
where she went?

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:22.702
She just ran off down there.

00:26:22.781 --> 00:26:24.373
I'm-I'm going to go
look for her.

00:26:24.449 --> 00:26:26.576
Uncle John?

00:26:26.651 --> 00:26:28.312
Yeah?

00:26:28.386 --> 00:26:30.616
I... it...

00:26:31.656 --> 00:26:33.180
B'Elanna.

00:26:33.258 --> 00:26:34.486
Where have you been?

00:26:35.927 --> 00:26:37.690
I'm sorry.

00:26:37.762 --> 00:26:39.923
I got kind of... separated.

00:26:40.065 --> 00:26:41.498
It was our fault.

00:26:41.566 --> 00:26:42.931
It was Dean's fault.

00:26:43.034 --> 00:26:45.161
He put a worm in her sandwich.

00:26:45.236 --> 00:26:47.500
I was just kidding.

00:26:47.572 --> 00:26:49.631
I'm really sorry.

00:26:49.708 --> 00:26:51.676
Forget it.

00:26:53.678 --> 00:26:56.613
Come on. Let's get
dinner started.

00:27:03.488 --> 00:27:05.888
You want to talk about it?

00:27:05.991 --> 00:27:07.117
I just wish...

00:27:07.192 --> 00:27:08.124
You wish what?

00:27:08.193 --> 00:27:09.854
I wish I weren't Klingon.

00:27:09.928 --> 00:27:11.828
Now, why would you say that?

00:27:11.896 --> 00:27:13.727
Because everyone
makes fun of me.

00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:15.060
Who's everyone?

00:27:15.133 --> 00:27:17.897
Dean, kids at school.

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:19.903
They all hate me.

00:27:20.972 --> 00:27:22.064
Did I ever tell you

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:24.734
what the kids at my school
used to call me?

00:27:26.411 --> 00:27:30.074
I used to fall asleep
in class all the time,

00:27:30.148 --> 00:27:33.845
so instead of John Torres,
they called me John "Snore-ez."

00:27:33.918 --> 00:27:36.113
It's not the same thing.

00:27:36.187 --> 00:27:37.552
Of course it is.

00:27:37.622 --> 00:27:38.816
Kids tease each other.

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:40.152
They can be very cruel,

00:27:40.225 --> 00:27:42.318
but it doesn't mean
that they hate you

00:27:42.394 --> 00:27:44.157
or that they hate Klingons.

00:27:44.229 --> 00:27:45.696
You don't understand!

00:27:45.764 --> 00:27:48.927
I think I do.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:52.197
You have to learn to be
a little less sensitive.

00:27:53.772 --> 00:27:55.535
Fine.

00:27:56.741 --> 00:27:58.675
Now come on.
Uncle Carl's going to tell

00:27:58.743 --> 00:28:00.335
one of his famous fish stories.

00:28:00.412 --> 00:28:03.210
I'd rather just read.

00:28:04.783 --> 00:28:06.751
Suit yourself.

00:28:13.425 --> 00:28:15.689
Did you know there
are fish around here

00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:16.692
that have wings?

00:28:16.761 --> 00:28:18.194
Flying fish?

00:28:18.263 --> 00:28:20.356
It's true. I'm telling you.
We saw one.

00:28:20.432 --> 00:28:21.524
Oh, yeah.

00:28:21.599 --> 00:28:23.032
Really?

00:28:23.101 --> 00:28:25.035
John, didn't we see
a flying fish today?

00:28:25.103 --> 00:28:26.365
We sure did.

00:28:26.438 --> 00:28:28.201
Jumped five feet in the air,
flew right into my lap.

00:28:28.273 --> 00:28:30.707
Oh, no!

00:28:30.775 --> 00:28:32.402
I jumped into
Uncle John's lap.

00:28:59.704 --> 00:29:01.331
Everybody asleep?

00:29:01.406 --> 00:29:04.102
They were exhausted.

00:29:04.175 --> 00:29:05.506
Coffee?

00:29:05.577 --> 00:29:06.737
Sure.

00:29:08.046 --> 00:29:09.513
Listen, I'm sorry.

00:29:09.581 --> 00:29:10.513
For what?

00:29:10.582 --> 00:29:12.447
The way Dean treated B'Elanna.

00:29:12.517 --> 00:29:13.745
I had a talk with him.

00:29:13.818 --> 00:29:17.515
He was just doing
what 11-year-olds do.

00:29:17.589 --> 00:29:21.389
I'm sure B'Elanna overreacted.

00:29:21.459 --> 00:29:23.893
What makes you say that?

00:29:23.962 --> 00:29:25.827
She's too damn sensitive.

00:29:25.897 --> 00:29:26.886
What do you mean?

00:29:26.965 --> 00:29:27.897
She's a great kid.

00:29:27.966 --> 00:29:29.433
You haven't been
around her much

00:29:29.501 --> 00:29:30.627
the last couple of years.

00:29:30.702 --> 00:29:35.230
She's gotten moody,
unpredictable, argumentative.

00:29:35.306 --> 00:29:36.398
Just like her mother.

00:29:36.474 --> 00:29:39.637
I thought you loved
Miral's... intensity.

00:29:39.711 --> 00:29:42.009
Everything's become
a fight with her.

00:29:42.080 --> 00:29:43.570
I guess the older I get,

00:29:43.648 --> 00:29:45.809
the less intensity
I can handle.

00:29:45.884 --> 00:29:46.908
You know, it's funny

00:29:47.018 --> 00:29:49.350
how Mom and Dad
always turn out to be right.

00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:50.648
What do you mean?

00:29:50.722 --> 00:29:53.657
Mom warned me
not to marry Miral.

00:29:53.725 --> 00:29:55.386
Mom loved Miral.

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:56.722
Sure, she did,

00:29:56.795 --> 00:30:00.162
but she never thought
I had the constitution

00:30:00.231 --> 00:30:02.426
to live with a Klingon...

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:05.435
and now I'm living
with two of them.

00:30:07.639 --> 00:30:09.300
Taya.

00:30:09.374 --> 00:30:11.069
What?

00:30:11.142 --> 00:30:14.737
"Taya." It's the feminine
form of "Chakotay."

00:30:14.813 --> 00:30:16.280
What do you think?

00:30:16.347 --> 00:30:17.939
I'll add it to the list,

00:30:18.016 --> 00:30:19.415
right after "Floxia."

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:20.576
Neelix suggested that one.

00:30:20.652 --> 00:30:21.914
It's number 32.

00:30:21.986 --> 00:30:23.613
On second thought,
you and Tom ought

00:30:23.688 --> 00:30:24.712
to come up with your own name.

00:30:26.291 --> 00:30:29.260
I knew there was a reason
I always liked you.

00:30:29.327 --> 00:30:32.057
You look like
you've been up all night.

00:30:32.130 --> 00:30:33.620
Want to get some coffee?

00:30:33.698 --> 00:30:36.223
That's the best offer
I've had all week.

00:30:38.670 --> 00:30:40.433
Morning.

00:30:40.505 --> 00:30:41.631
Hi.

00:30:41.706 --> 00:30:44.334
Join us for breakfast?

00:30:46.845 --> 00:30:47.777
You know what?

00:30:47.846 --> 00:30:48.813
I forgot my padd.

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:50.438
Why don't you two go ahead?

00:30:50.515 --> 00:30:51.812
I'll meet you in the Mess Hall.

00:30:53.852 --> 00:30:55.979
So, how are you today?

00:30:56.054 --> 00:31:00.388
I haven't changed my mind,
if that's what you mean.

00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:03.256
No, what I meant was,
how are you?

00:31:03.328 --> 00:31:06.388
I've been better,
but I'll get over it.

00:31:06.464 --> 00:31:12.061
You know, Harry has the
lumpiest pillows on the ship.

00:31:12.136 --> 00:31:16.163
He snores, keeps
the room way too hot.

00:31:18.476 --> 00:31:19.773
I missed you.

00:31:19.844 --> 00:31:22.711
Me, too.

00:31:24.816 --> 00:31:27.717
I still owe you that slice
of peanut butter toast.

00:31:27.785 --> 00:31:31.221
Why don't we go back to our
quarters, fire up the toaster?

00:31:31.289 --> 00:31:32.449
Sounds nice.

00:31:32.523 --> 00:31:35.219
Lieutenant Torres,
Lieutenant Paris,

00:31:35.293 --> 00:31:36.988
please report to Sick Bay.

00:31:40.164 --> 00:31:41.859
I've reviewed
the data you gave me,

00:31:41.933 --> 00:31:43.730
and I've also done
my own analysis.

00:31:43.801 --> 00:31:45.132
Skip the details, Doctor.

00:31:45.203 --> 00:31:48.434
You've already made it clear
what you think of my proposal.

00:31:48.506 --> 00:31:50.565
Actually, I've
changed my opinion.

00:31:50.642 --> 00:31:51.574
What?

00:31:51.643 --> 00:31:54.305
The genetic alterations
you've suggested

00:31:54.379 --> 00:31:55.747
are necessary.

00:31:55.813 --> 00:31:58.145
On what grounds?

00:31:58.216 --> 00:32:01.982
The "clash" I mentioned between
Klingon and human metabolism.

00:32:02.053 --> 00:32:04.248
It's more extensive
than I realized.

00:32:04.322 --> 00:32:05.653
How extensive?

00:32:05.723 --> 00:32:06.917
Theoretically,

00:32:07.025 --> 00:32:09.585
it could lead
to complete metabolic failure.

00:32:09.661 --> 00:32:11.151
But you can fix it?

00:32:11.229 --> 00:32:12.355
By eliminating

00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:14.159
most of her Klingon
genetic material.

00:32:14.232 --> 00:32:16.166
Are you sure about all of this?

00:32:16.234 --> 00:32:17.929
My analysis was quite thorough.

00:32:18.069 --> 00:32:20.663
Of course, if our
circumstances were different,

00:32:20.738 --> 00:32:23.206
you would be free to seek
a second opinion.

00:32:23.274 --> 00:32:24.605
No offense, Doc,

00:32:24.676 --> 00:32:28.942
but I am just trying
to understand what's going on.

00:32:29.047 --> 00:32:30.947
You're welcome
to review my findings,

00:32:31.015 --> 00:32:32.846
but let me stress

00:32:32.917 --> 00:32:35.852
it would be unwise
to delay this too long.

00:32:35.920 --> 00:32:36.944
Why?

00:32:37.055 --> 00:32:38.317
The fetus is at a critical

00:32:38.389 --> 00:32:39.549
stage of development.

00:32:39.624 --> 00:32:41.216
Antibodies have begun to form.

00:32:44.362 --> 00:32:45.829
How long do we have?

00:32:45.897 --> 00:32:48.627
I've scheduled the procedure
for tomorrow morning,

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:49.894
with your permission.

00:32:57.175 --> 00:32:58.403
I want to thank you both

00:32:58.476 --> 00:33:00.444
for helping B'Elanna
when she fainted.

00:33:00.511 --> 00:33:02.103
I'm glad it wasn't a parasite.

00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:03.511
Well, you probably

00:33:03.581 --> 00:33:05.105
don't know this,
but there may be

00:33:05.183 --> 00:33:06.707
some problems
with the pregnancy.

00:33:06.784 --> 00:33:08.183
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:33:08.252 --> 00:33:11.517
The Doctor suggested
a treatment for the baby,

00:33:11.589 --> 00:33:14.717
but his findings are very
confusing... at least to me.

00:33:14.792 --> 00:33:16.657
You have
some expertise in genetics.

00:33:16.728 --> 00:33:18.491
Do you mind taking
a look at this?

00:33:18.563 --> 00:33:19.791
Of course not.

00:33:19.864 --> 00:33:21.855
Whatever the problem is,

00:33:21.933 --> 00:33:25.801
I have no doubt
the Doctor will solve it.

00:33:25.870 --> 00:33:27.360
I hope you're right.

00:33:27.438 --> 00:33:29.770
Your confusion
is understandable.

00:33:29.841 --> 00:33:31.934
There's a
computational error.

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:35.138
It's not like the Doctor
to make a mistake.

00:33:35.213 --> 00:33:36.840
I didn't think
that was possible,

00:33:36.914 --> 00:33:39.576
unless there's some sort
of glitch in his program.

00:33:39.650 --> 00:33:40.912
I'll run a diagnostic.

00:33:40.985 --> 00:33:42.418
Thank you.

00:33:42.487 --> 00:33:44.546
Please tell Lieutenant Torres

00:33:44.622 --> 00:33:46.886
if there's anything I can do...

00:33:46.958 --> 00:33:49.051
I'll let her know. Thanks.

00:33:49.127 --> 00:33:50.424
It appears to be

00:33:50.495 --> 00:33:51.723
more than a glitch.

00:33:51.796 --> 00:33:55.288
I believe the Doctor's program
has been tampered with.

00:33:57.502 --> 00:34:00.130
B'Elanna, this is Tom. Respond.

00:34:00.204 --> 00:34:03.037
Computer,
locate Lieutenant Torres.

00:34:03.107 --> 00:34:05.598
Lieutenant Torres
is in Sick Bay.

00:34:08.579 --> 00:34:09.603
Frankly, I'm relieved

00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:12.046
you decided not to wait
till the last minute.

00:34:12.116 --> 00:34:15.483
Once this is behind us,
I'm sure we'll all feel better.

00:34:21.993 --> 00:34:24.928
Someone's blocked
communications to Sick Bay.

00:34:25.029 --> 00:34:27.759
See if you can
deactivate the Doctor.

00:34:27.832 --> 00:34:30.062
Access to his program
has been restricted.

00:34:30.134 --> 00:34:31.431
Keep trying.

00:34:31.502 --> 00:34:32.434
Paris to Tuvok.

00:34:32.503 --> 00:34:33.435
Go ahead.

00:34:33.504 --> 00:34:35.495
Meet me in Sick Bay.

00:34:35.573 --> 00:34:37.632
Why would she alter
the Doctor's program?

00:34:37.708 --> 00:34:38.766
To change his mind

00:34:38.843 --> 00:34:40.208
about the medical procedure.

00:34:40.278 --> 00:34:42.610
Computer, open Sick Bay doors.

00:34:42.680 --> 00:34:44.272
Unable to comply.

00:34:45.750 --> 00:34:49.618
Override.
Authorization: Tuvok-pi-alpha.

00:34:49.687 --> 00:34:52.155
Authorization denied.

00:34:57.028 --> 00:34:58.757
Doctor, stop
what you're doing.

00:34:58.830 --> 00:35:01.424
You're interrupting
a medical procedure.

00:35:01.499 --> 00:35:03.228
Your program
has been altered.

00:35:03.301 --> 00:35:04.791
What do you mean, altered?

00:35:04.869 --> 00:35:06.427
Ignore him.

00:35:06.504 --> 00:35:08.096
B'Elanna, this
is completely irrational.

00:35:08.172 --> 00:35:10.436
Will someone please tell me
what's going on?

00:35:10.508 --> 00:35:12.271
I'm your patient.
Your first duty

00:35:12.343 --> 00:35:13.571
is to me and my baby.

00:35:13.644 --> 00:35:14.702
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:35:14.779 --> 00:35:15.837
Kim here.

00:35:15.913 --> 00:35:17.676
There's a force field
in Sick Bay.

00:35:17.748 --> 00:35:18.772
I can't deactivate it.

00:35:18.850 --> 00:35:20.112
Cut power to the EPS relay

00:35:20.184 --> 00:35:21.913
surrounding the Surgical Bay.

00:35:22.019 --> 00:35:24.180
Access has been restricted.

00:35:24.255 --> 00:35:25.745
I'll have to bypass them.

00:35:25.823 --> 00:35:28.519
You said it could be dangerous
to delay the procedure.

00:35:28.593 --> 00:35:30.925
She's manipulating you, Doc,
in more ways than one.

00:35:31.028 --> 00:35:32.052
I'm sorry, Lieutenant,

00:35:32.130 --> 00:35:34.189
but if there's something
wrong with my program...

00:35:34.265 --> 00:35:36.597
There's nothing wrong
with your program!

00:35:36.667 --> 00:35:39.397
I'm cutting power
to the Surgical Bay now.

00:35:42.707 --> 00:35:44.368
I suggest we deactivate
your program,

00:35:44.442 --> 00:35:48.469
until we determine
the extent of the alterations.

00:35:50.381 --> 00:35:51.939
I understand.

00:35:52.083 --> 00:35:54.483
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:35:55.553 --> 00:35:57.851
You had no right to interfere.

00:35:57.955 --> 00:36:00.549
Tuvok, would you mind
giving us a minute?

00:36:06.063 --> 00:36:07.428
I never thought

00:36:07.498 --> 00:36:09.056
you would go this far.

00:36:09.133 --> 00:36:10.828
I don't know what
you're talking about.

00:36:10.902 --> 00:36:13.063
Reprogramming the Doctor?

00:36:13.137 --> 00:36:14.729
I upgraded his program,

00:36:14.805 --> 00:36:17.433
so he could understand
what had to be done.

00:36:17.508 --> 00:36:19.601
You mean
to reconfigure our baby

00:36:19.677 --> 00:36:22.111
so she wouldn't be
treated like a monster.

00:36:22.180 --> 00:36:25.047
It's not just about the
way she'll be treated!

00:36:25.116 --> 00:36:26.083
What else

00:36:26.150 --> 00:36:27.242
is it about, then?!

00:36:27.318 --> 00:36:29.183
Come on, B'Elanna, tell me!

00:36:29.253 --> 00:36:31.084
Forget it.

00:36:31.155 --> 00:36:32.918
No, no. We're not
going to forget it.

00:36:32.990 --> 00:36:34.821
We're going to talk
about this right now.

00:36:34.892 --> 00:36:36.154
Stop telling me what to do!

00:36:36.227 --> 00:36:37.421
You're not my father!

00:36:42.066 --> 00:36:44.000
What are you talking about?

00:36:46.837 --> 00:36:48.270
Look, my fath...

00:36:49.340 --> 00:36:51.501
What?

00:36:51.576 --> 00:36:53.476
What about him?

00:36:54.946 --> 00:36:57.938
We were inseparable.

00:36:58.082 --> 00:37:01.347
He spoiled me
and I worshipped him,

00:37:01.419 --> 00:37:03.546
but the older I got...

00:37:03.621 --> 00:37:06.749
we just grew apart.

00:37:09.560 --> 00:37:14.463
He ended up organizing this
camping trip with my cousins.

00:37:14.532 --> 00:37:17.296
I guess he just wanted to...

00:37:17.368 --> 00:37:20.895
I don't know...
make things better again.

00:37:20.972 --> 00:37:22.234
But it didn't.

00:37:22.306 --> 00:37:24.274
It was awful.

00:37:26.611 --> 00:37:28.545
I ended up trying to run away.

00:37:28.613 --> 00:37:30.911
B'Elanna?

00:37:30.982 --> 00:37:32.506
What are you doing?

00:37:32.583 --> 00:37:35.381
It was so stupid.

00:37:35.453 --> 00:37:38.911
I mean, where was I going to go?

00:37:39.056 --> 00:37:42.219
You probably just
wanted him to stop you.

00:37:44.495 --> 00:37:46.588
Well, he did.

00:37:46.664 --> 00:37:48.655
Don't touch me.

00:37:48.733 --> 00:37:50.564
B'Elanna, what's wrong?

00:37:50.635 --> 00:37:52.603
You know what's wrong.

00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:54.900
No, I don't.

00:37:54.972 --> 00:37:58.840
Maybe I'm just being moody
and unpredictable.

00:37:58.909 --> 00:38:00.774
What are you talking about?

00:38:00.845 --> 00:38:03.405
I heard what you said
to Uncle Carl.

00:38:05.850 --> 00:38:09.286
You shouldn't be listening
to private conversations.

00:38:09.353 --> 00:38:11.913
And you shouldn't have said
what you did about Mommy!

00:38:30.641 --> 00:38:31.699
B'Elanna...

00:38:31.776 --> 00:38:33.107
listen to me.

00:38:33.177 --> 00:38:36.078
Your mother and I
are having problems, but...

00:38:36.147 --> 00:38:38.047
You don't love her anymore.

00:38:38.115 --> 00:38:39.412
That's not true.

00:38:39.483 --> 00:38:41.417
Yes, it is,
and you don't love me, either.

00:38:41.485 --> 00:38:42.417
B'Elanna...

00:38:42.486 --> 00:38:43.418
You're no different

00:38:43.487 --> 00:38:44.545
than anyone else.

00:38:44.622 --> 00:38:45.919
You don't like Klingons.
You said it.

00:38:46.057 --> 00:38:48.617
You are twisting my words,
B'Elanna.

00:38:48.693 --> 00:38:49.785
Maybe he was right.

00:38:49.860 --> 00:38:51.225
Maybe you misunderstood.

00:38:51.295 --> 00:38:53.490
No, I know what I heard.

00:38:53.564 --> 00:38:54.792
It made me so angry!

00:38:54.865 --> 00:38:57.493
You had a right to be,
after the things he said.

00:38:57.568 --> 00:38:59.536
It's not what he said.

00:38:59.603 --> 00:39:01.230
It's what I said.

00:39:01.305 --> 00:39:02.863
If you can't stand living
with us,

00:39:03.007 --> 00:39:04.736
then why don't you just leave?!

00:39:06.610 --> 00:39:09.636
And that's exactly what he did.

00:39:09.714 --> 00:39:11.079
Oh, B'Elanna...

00:39:11.148 --> 00:39:14.879
12 days later...

00:39:14.985 --> 00:39:17.613
and he never came back.

00:39:17.688 --> 00:39:20.122
You can't blame yourself
for that.

00:39:20.191 --> 00:39:21.783
Why not?

00:39:21.859 --> 00:39:27.354
Because... he was obviously
unhappy about his marriage.

00:39:27.431 --> 00:39:30.025
He didn't leave
just because you told him to.

00:39:30.101 --> 00:39:32.092
You don't know that.

00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:35.798
Look, whatever the reason was,

00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:40.810
I'm sure it was a horrible thing
for you to live with.

00:39:47.385 --> 00:39:48.352
Wait a minute.

00:39:48.419 --> 00:39:49.511
You don't think...

00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:53.721
B'Elanna,

00:39:53.791 --> 00:39:55.918
I am never going
to leave you.

00:39:55.993 --> 00:39:59.190
You say that now...

00:39:59.263 --> 00:40:02.232
but think about how hard it is
to live with one Klingon.

00:40:02.299 --> 00:40:03.857
Pretty soon it'll be two.

00:40:03.934 --> 00:40:07.461
And someday I hope
it's three or four.

00:40:07.538 --> 00:40:09.335
I mean it,

00:40:09.407 --> 00:40:15.175
and I hope that every one
of them is just like you.

00:40:15.246 --> 00:40:17.942
B'Elanna...

00:40:18.082 --> 00:40:19.913
I am not your father,

00:40:19.984 --> 00:40:22.077
and you are not your mother,

00:40:22.153 --> 00:40:24.849
and our daughter
is going to be perfect

00:40:24.922 --> 00:40:26.856
just the way she is.

00:40:26.924 --> 00:40:29.188
You really think so?

00:40:29.260 --> 00:40:32.388
I know so.

00:40:40.905 --> 00:40:45.535
Medical Officer's Log,
Stardate 54452.6.

00:40:45.609 --> 00:40:48.737
Lieutenant Torres
has deleted the alterations

00:40:48.813 --> 00:40:50.644
she made to my program.

00:40:50.714 --> 00:40:54.377
It's a relief to be back
to my old self again.

00:40:54.452 --> 00:40:56.579
Good morning, Lieutenant.

00:40:56.654 --> 00:40:57.848
You're not
feeling ill, are you?

00:40:57.922 --> 00:40:58.980
No.

00:40:59.089 --> 00:41:01.557
I'm fine.

00:41:01.625 --> 00:41:07.086
I just wanted to apologize
for violating your program.

00:41:09.934 --> 00:41:12.198
Apology accepted.

00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:16.797
Not guilty by reason
of biochemistry.

00:41:16.874 --> 00:41:19.775
Nice of you to let
me off the hook,

00:41:19.844 --> 00:41:23.940
but biochemistry
isn't an excuse.

00:41:24.048 --> 00:41:27.142
I knew exactly
what I was doing.

00:41:30.354 --> 00:41:31.946
Is something wrong?

00:41:32.022 --> 00:41:34.388
I don't know.

00:41:39.563 --> 00:41:42.361
Your baby's kicking.

00:41:42.433 --> 00:41:43.957
So soon?

00:41:44.068 --> 00:41:45.535
Well, she is part Klingon.

00:41:47.104 --> 00:41:49.072
There it is again.

00:41:51.842 --> 00:41:53.173
May I?

00:42:00.317 --> 00:42:02.547
Feisty little thing, isn't she?

00:42:02.620 --> 00:42:05.088
I wonder where
she gets that from.

00:42:05.155 --> 00:42:06.383
Speaking of the baby,

00:42:06.457 --> 00:42:08.288
I have another request.

00:42:08.359 --> 00:42:11.556
Yes?

00:42:11.629 --> 00:42:14.621
I wonder if you'd
like to be her godfather.

00:42:16.667 --> 00:42:18.396
Neelix wants the job,

00:42:18.469 --> 00:42:20.437
but he's already got
Naomi Wildman,

00:42:20.504 --> 00:42:23.200
and Chakotay knows less
about raising kids than Harry,

00:42:23.274 --> 00:42:24.434
and, and if you think...

00:42:24.508 --> 00:42:25.440
I accept.

00:42:25.509 --> 00:42:27.340
Thanks.

00:42:27.411 --> 00:42:29.936
Thank you.

00:42:30.080 --> 00:42:33.641
I was also wondering...

00:42:33.717 --> 00:42:36.880
Do you think I could
see her one more time?

00:42:36.954 --> 00:42:39.514
The holographic projection,
I mean.

00:42:39.590 --> 00:42:41.319
I don't see why not.

00:43:00.644 --> 00:43:02.874
She is cute, isn't she?
